<title>POLAND: Kety soars on likely aluminium demand rise.</title>
<headline>Kety soars on likely aluminium demand rise.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in the Polish aluminium plant Kety SA jumped 9.8 percent to 206.5 zlotys in high 9.6 million zloty turnover on possible aluminium demand growth in Poland, traders said.</p>
<p>They said investors expected the demand to rise after Japan's Isuzu Motors Ltd said on Wednesday it was studying the feasibility of producing diesel engines in Europe.</p>
<p>A Japanese daily has earlier said Isuzu planned to invest 50 billion yen to produce diesel engines in Poland at an annual rate of 300,000 units.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
